{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00521",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.98,
      "end_seconds": 11.88,
      "duration_seconds": 10.9,
      "text": "Hello doctor. I am having this redness on my face only, since two years now. It is not going, and I am feeling very conscious."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 13.53,
      "end_seconds": 21.59,
      "duration_seconds": 8.06,
      "text": "Okay, Mrs. Raghunathan. Sit down. Show me where it is worst, and tell me what you notice."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 24.18,
      "end_seconds": 38.08,
      "duration_seconds": 13.9,
      "text": "Here, on both cheeks and the nose. It is... how to say, it is red like I am blushing always. And sometimes on the forehead also."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 40.11,
      "end_seconds": 50.03,
      "duration_seconds": 9.92,
      "text": "Red cheeks and nose, since two years. Does the redness stay all day, or does it come in waves?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 52.45,
      "end_seconds": 65.02,
      "duration_seconds": 12.57,
      "text": "Waves, mostly. It becomes too much when I drink hot tea or when I eat spicy food. Then my face is... flushing, flushing like a heater."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 67.63,
      "end_seconds": 74.8,
      "duration_seconds": 7.17,
      "text": "So hot drinks and spicy food set off the flushing. Anything else that triggers it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 75.45,
      "end_seconds": 81.14,
      "duration_seconds": 5.69,
      "text": "Sun, also. And in the kitchen, when I am standing near the stove."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 82.15,
      "end_seconds": 88.87,
      "duration_seconds": 6.72,
      "text": "Sun and heat. Is there any pain with it, or a burning feeling?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 90.1,
      "end_seconds": 96.42,
      "duration_seconds": 6.32,
      "text": "Burning, yes. Like a stinging, especially after washing my face with soap."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 97.33,
      "end_seconds": 102.66,
      "duration_seconds": 5.33,
      "text": "Okay. Are there any spots, bumps, or pimples along with the redness?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 105.23,
      "end_seconds": 111.92,
      "duration_seconds": 6.69,
      "text": "Small bumps, yes, a few. Like pimples, but no head on them. They come and go."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 113.25,
      "end_seconds": 117.92,
      "duration_seconds": 4.67,
      "text": "Any itching, joint pains or fevers with this?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 119.84,
      "end_seconds": 126.0,
      "duration_seconds": 6.16,
      "text": "No, no itching. No joint pains, no fever. Nothing like that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 128.11,
      "end_seconds": 133.56,
      "duration_seconds": 5.45,
      "text": "Good. What about your eyes? Any dryness, redness or blurred vision?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 135.47,
      "end_seconds": 139.99,
      "duration_seconds": 4.52,
      "text": "No, eyes are fine, doctor. Nothing in the eyes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 141.46,
      "end_seconds": 148.97,
      "duration_seconds": 7.51,
      "text": "Alright. Now, what medicines are you using right now, for the face or anything else?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 150.55,
      "end_seconds": 159.19,
      "duration_seconds": 8.64,
      "text": "For the face, I am using the metronidazole gel, twice a day. And at night the azelaic acid cream."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 161.83,
      "end_seconds": 167.8,
      "duration_seconds": 5.97,
      "text": "Metronidazole gel twice a day, azelaic acid at night. Any tablets?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 170.44,
      "end_seconds": 178.85,
      "duration_seconds": 8.41,
      "text": "Yes, metformin, 500 mg, morning and night. And levothyroxine, 50 micrograms, every morning on empty stomach."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 180.05,
      "end_seconds": 184.31,
      "duration_seconds": 4.26,
      "text": "Metformin and levothyroxine. And for what conditions are those?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 186.45,
      "end_seconds": 192.14,
      "duration_seconds": 5.69,
      "text": "Type 2 diabetes, since some years. And thyroid, underactive thyroid, I have."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 194.14,
      "end_seconds": 202.33,
      "duration_seconds": 8.19,
      "text": "Type 2 diabetes and an underactive thyroid. Fine. Do you have any allergies to medicines or creams?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 204.16,
      "end_seconds": 211.11,
      "duration_seconds": 6.95,
      "text": "No, no allergies. I am using everything without problem, only this redness is not going."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 212.36,
      "end_seconds": 215.83,
      "duration_seconds": 3.47,
      "text": "Good. Any operations in the past?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 216.66,
      "end_seconds": 224.5,
      "duration_seconds": 7.84,
      "text": "Appendix I got removed when I was twelve years old. And the gallbladder, in 2015."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 226.84,
      "end_seconds": 234.65,
      "duration_seconds": 7.81,
      "text": "Appendix at twelve, gallbladder in 2015. Does anyone in your family have skin problems like this?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 235.48,
      "end_seconds": 244.9,
      "duration_seconds": 9.42,
      "text": "My mother had rosacea. Same red face. She also never went to doctor, she only used home remedies."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 246.78,
      "end_seconds": 252.52,
      "duration_seconds": 5.74,
      "text": "That's useful. Now a few questions about your lifestyle. Do you smoke?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 254.01,
      "end_seconds": 257.55,
      "duration_seconds": 3.54,
      "text": "Never. I never smoked, not even once."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 258.5,
      "end_seconds": 259.97,
      "duration_seconds": 1.47,
      "text": "And alcohol?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 261.3,
      "end_seconds": 267.92,
      "duration_seconds": 6.62,
      "text": "Occasionally only, a glass of wine on weekends. That is all."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 269.62,
      "end_seconds": 272.55,
      "duration_seconds": 2.93,
      "text": "What work do you do?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 274.54,
      "end_seconds": 282.19,
      "duration_seconds": 7.65,
      "text": "I am a school teacher. Primary class, so playground duty in the sun also."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 283.12,
      "end_seconds": 285.86,
      "duration_seconds": 2.74,
      "text": "Do you exercise at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 286.94,
      "end_seconds": 294.47,
      "duration_seconds": 7.53,
      "text": "I walk every morning, forty minutes. In the sun, sir, at seven o'clock only. Is it bad?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 303.85,
      "end_seconds": 311.97,
      "duration_seconds": 8.12,
      "text": "Early enough to be mild. Let me take your readings first. Blood pressure is 126 over 80."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 313.86,
      "end_seconds": 322.15,
      "duration_seconds": 8.29,
      "text": "Pulse is 76, temperature 36.8 degrees, oxygen saturation 98 percent. Your weight is 72 kilograms."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 324.32,
      "end_seconds": 325.64,
      "duration_seconds": 1.32,
      "text": "Everything normal?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 334.59,
      "end_seconds": 345.71,
      "duration_seconds": 11.12,
      "text": "All normal. Now let me look at your face under the light. Please face me, and keep your eyes closed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 356.08,
      "end_seconds": 364.27,
      "duration_seconds": 8.19,
      "text": "There is redness across both cheeks and the nose, with a few small red bumps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 365.52,
      "end_seconds": 372.71,
      "duration_seconds": 7.19,
      "text": "I don't see any blackheads, so this is most likely rosacea, rather than acne."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 374.18,
      "end_seconds": 379.3,
      "duration_seconds": 5.12,
      "text": "Rosacea, like my mother. Will it go away completely?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 381.15,
      "end_seconds": 395.8,
      "duration_seconds": 14.65,
      "text": "It's long-term, but it can be controlled well. The first step is protecting the skin. Use a sunscreen every morning, SPF 30 at least, and a gentle cleanser instead of soap."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 398.08,
      "end_seconds": 404.28,
      "duration_seconds": 6.2,
      "text": "Even in the kitchen, near the stove? I cannot avoid that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 406.74,
      "end_seconds": 414.67,
      "duration_seconds": 7.93,
      "text": "Do what you can. Keep your face back from the steam, and let the tea cool first."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 415.57,
      "end_seconds": 421.59,
      "duration_seconds": 6.02,
      "text": "I will try. Should I stop the gel and cream, then?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 424.15,
      "end_seconds": 438.09,
      "duration_seconds": 13.94,
      "text": "No, continue both as you are. I'd like to order liver function tests, since you're on metformin and thyroid medicine and we may adjust treatment later."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 440.08,
      "end_seconds": 447.05,
      "duration_seconds": 6.97,
      "text": "Fine. I had my blood sugar test done last month, only. Should I bring that report?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 448.39,
      "end_seconds": 462.18,
      "duration_seconds": 13.79,
      "text": "Yes, please bring it. I'd also like to book a patch test, to see whether any cream or cosmetic is aggravating your skin, small patches on the back for two days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 463.87,
      "end_seconds": 475.03,
      "duration_seconds": 11.16,
      "text": "One more thing. If the redness doesn't settle with all this, we might consider a small skin biopsy to be sure of the diagnosis."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 477.54,
      "end_seconds": 482.24,
      "duration_seconds": 4.7,
      "text": "Biopsy? That is cutting the skin? I am afraid."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 484.43,
      "end_seconds": 493.92,
      "duration_seconds": 9.49,
      "text": "It's only a tiny sample under local anaesthetic, and only if we need it. Not now. Let's see how you respond first."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 494.78,
      "end_seconds": 498.61,
      "duration_seconds": 3.83,
      "text": "Okay. When should I come again?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 499.89,
      "end_seconds": 505.38,
      "duration_seconds": 5.49,
      "text": "Come back in six weeks, with the test results ready."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 507.32,
      "end_seconds": 514.76,
      "duration_seconds": 7.44,
      "text": "Six weeks. Thank you, doctor. I was very worried, I thought it is something serious."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 515.96,
      "end_seconds": 525.04,
      "duration_seconds": 9.08,
      "text": "It's not dangerous. Keep a diary of what triggers the flushing, that will help us a lot. Take care."
    }
  ]
}
